# TRP3 Profile Viewer

A browser-only viewer for Total RP 3 (TRP3) character profiles. Paste a TRP3
export string and it decodes the LibSerialize payload, then renders the profile
in two styles: a clean **Simple View** and an **In-Game View** that mimics the
WoW client.

No build step. Open `index.html` directly.


## Interface

The welcome screen introduces the import workflow. `design.css` contains the
responsive interface styling; theme palettes remain in `theme.js`. Menus open
with click or keyboard activation. Dialogs support Escape, keep keyboard focus
inside while open, and restore focus on close.

## File layout

Scripts are plain (non-module) files that share one global namespace, `window.TRP3`.
**Load order in `index.html` matters**, because each file attaches to `TRP3`:

| Order | File | Responsibility |
|-------|------|----------------|
| 0 | `assets.js` | Embedded essential artwork for browser and direct-file export |
| 1 | `theme.js`  | Class themes, `TRP3.defaults`, `applyTheme`, shared state/actions bootstrap |
| 2 | `format.js` | **Texture/icon resolution** + TRP3 markup formatter (Simple/In-Game) |
| 3 | `core.js`   | LibSerialize token codec + token stream -> profile object parser |
| 4 | `render.js` | View layer: modals, tabs, edit mode, DOM painting, `data-action` dispatch |
| 5 | `app.js`    | Boot, import pipeline, history storage, exports (TRP3 / Discord / PNG) |

Everything is wired through delegated `data-action` attributes (see `render.js`
`dispatchAction`); no functions are attached to `window` directly.


## Texture & icon resolution  (`format.js`)

TRP3 markup and profile fields reference WoW textures by their **in-game path**,
e.g. `Interface\QuestionFrame\answer-ChromieScenario-Hourglass`. Browsers can't
load those paths, so they are mapped to two different public hosts.

### The two hosts

```js
const ICON_CDN    = 'https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/large/';
const DEFAULT_ICON = TRP3.bundledImages['assets/icons/questionmark.jpg'];

const TEXTURE_CDN = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/Gethe/wow-ui-textures@live/';
```

* **`ICON_CDN` (Wowhead)** - for spell/ability/item **icons**. Keyed by bare icon
  *name*, `.jpg`, and **case-insensitive** (`getIconUrl` lowercases for you).
* **`TEXTURE_CDN` (jsDelivr -> GitHub mirror)** - for everything else: banners,
  backgrounds, frames, atlases, etc. `Gethe/wow-ui-textures` is a git mirror of
  Blizzard's `Interface\` art already converted from `.blp` to `.png`, laid out
  with the same folder tree. **Case-sensitive.**

### Path mapping rules (`getTextureUrl`)

Given an interface texture path:

1. `\` -> `/`
2. strip a leading `Interface/`
3. strip any `.blp` / `.tga` / `.png` / `.jpg` extension
4. append **`.PNG`** (the mirror always uses uppercase `.PNG`)

```
Interface\QuestionFrame\answer-ChromieScenario-Hourglass
  -> https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/Gethe/wow-ui-textures@live/QuestionFrame/answer-ChromieScenario-Hourglass.PNG

Interface\TALENTFRAME\bg-mage-frost.blp
  -> https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/Gethe/wow-ui-textures@live/TALENTFRAME/bg-mage-frost.PNG
```

### Which host is used? (`isIconPath` / `resolveImageUrl`)

A reference is treated as an **icon** when it has no folder (`inv_misc_gear_01`)
or its **first** folder is `Icons\` (e.g. `Interface\Icons\...`). Everything else
goes to the texture mirror - note this includes art folders that merely *contain*
an `Icons` subfolder, such as `Interface\PVPFrame\Icons\prestige-icon-3-3`, which
is interface art and 404s on the Wowhead icon CDN.

`resolveImageUrl(path)` returns `{ src, fallback }`:

| Input kind | `src` | `fallback` |
|------------|-------|------------|
| icon name / `Interface\Icons\...` | `ICON_CDN` | `DEFAULT_ICON` |
| interface texture | `TEXTURE_CDN` | `ICON_CDN` (last resort) |

`{img:...}` tags inside the About text are rendered with this resolver (in
`formatInGameView`). Attribute, trait, personality, and portrait icons use
`getIconUrl` directly, since those are always real icons.

The emitted `<img>` has an inline `onerror` (`fallbackHandler`) that swaps to the
fallback URL once, then hides the element if that also fails. `attrUrl` strips
quote/angle characters so a hostile path cannot break out of the `src`/`onerror`
attributes.

### Textures missing from the mirror (`TEXTURE_OVERRIDES`)

The `Gethe/wow-ui-textures` `live` branch is **frozen at 9.2.7 (Aug 2022)**, so
any texture added in **Dragonflight or later** 404s there - most visibly the
`Expansion09` loading screens. `format.js` keeps a small path -> URL override map
for these:

```js
const TEXTURE_OVERRIDES = {
  'glues/loadingscreens/expansion09/main/loadscreen_mappirate':
      'assets/textures/loadscreen-mappirate.webp',
};
```

The map banner is bundled from its game texture to avoid the wiki host's
hotlink and CORS restrictions. `assets.js` supplies embedded image data so the
same artwork also exports when opening `index.html` directly via `file://`.
See "Bundled artwork sources" below for artwork provenance.

* Keys are the path **normalised to lower-case**, `Interface\` stripped, no
  extension (that's `normalizeTexturePath`).
* `getTextureUrl` and `resolveImageUrl` consult the map first; an override that
  fails falls back to `DEFAULT_ICON`.
* Add entries at runtime with `TRP3.setTextureOverride(path, url)`.

**Adding a new override.** There is no path-based PNG host for DF+ art. Options,
best first: (1) find a direct `.jpg`/`.png` URL for that specific art (community
wikis often have them, e.g. loading screens - use the plain `/images/<File>` URL);
(2) fetch the raw `.blp` from **wago.tools** and convert it yourself. wago.tools
exposes a CORS-enabled API:

```bash
# build -> fileDataID lookup needs the 150 MB community listfile (path;fdid):
curl -sL https://github.com/wowdev/wow-listfile/releases/latest/download/community-listfile.csv
# e.g. -> 5580542;interface/glues/loadingscreens/expansion09/main/loadscreen_mappirate.blp
# then the file bytes (raw BLP, not PNG) with Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *:
curl -s "https://wago.tools/api/casc/5580542" -o banner.blp
```

Because a path -> fdid lookup needs the full listfile and the result is a raw BLP
(no server-side PNG conversion), a fully general DF+ resolver is **not
implemented**; curated overrides are the intended stopgap.


## Updating / maintaining the resolver

**New game content (patches, expansions).** The mirror is frozen at 9.2.7, so
textures newer than that will **404** - add a `TEXTURE_OVERRIDES` entry (above).
Textures on or before 9.2.7 are served as-is; jsDelivr caches GitHub files for
~7 days, so to force a refresh of one file:

```bash
curl "https://purge.jsdelivr.net/gh/Gethe/wow-ui-textures@live/QuestionFrame/answer-ChromieScenario-Hourglass.PNG"
```

If you need a frozen snapshot instead of `live`, pin a commit/tag in
`TEXTURE_CDN` (`...wow-ui-textures@<sha>/`).

**A texture 404s but exists in-game.** Almost always a **case mismatch**
(`Icons` vs `ICONS`, `answer-...` vs `Answer-...`). Check the real filename via
the GitHub API and keep the exact casing:

```bash
curl -s "https://api.github.com/repos/Gethe/wow-ui-textures/contents/QuestionFrame?ref=live" \
  | grep -o '"name": "[^"]*"'
```

If a case-insensitive fallback is ever needed, the full tree is ~67k files / ~21 MB
(`.../git/trees/live?recursive=1`) and could be fetched once and cached to build
a lowercase-name -> real-path index. Not currently implemented.

**Host is down or rate-limited.** Swap `TEXTURE_CDN` for another mirror; both are
verified working with the same path layout:

```js
const TEXTURE_CDN = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Gethe/wow-ui-textures/live/';
const TEXTURE_CDN = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/syl404/wow-textures@live/';
```

**New icon fallback.** Change `DEFAULT_ICON` (currently
`inv_misc_questionmark.jpg`). Wowhead icon paths are `<name>.jpg` under
`ICON_CDN`; any spell/item icon name works.

**TRP3's own textures are NOT on the mirror.** The addon ships its own art in
`totalRP3/Resources/` (`.tga`/`.blp`/`.png`: `trp3logo`, the `ui-*` frame pieces,
`ui-list-bullet-*`, the minimap `trp3minimap.tga`, etc.). If you need those,
convert them to PNG and host/bundle them yourself, then special-case them in
`resolveImageUrl` before the `TEXTURE_CDN` lookup.

### Quick verification

```bash
# Should return: HTTP 200  image/png
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code} %{content_type}\n" \
  -L "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/Gethe/wow-ui-textures@live/QuestionFrame/answer-ChromieScenario-Hourglass.PNG"
```

### Not yet implemented

The profile's **About-frame tiled background** (`data.BK`, an index into TRP3's
`tiledBackgrounds` list) is not rendered - `core.js` doesn't parse it yet. To add
it, resolve the index to its `bgFile` and render it with `getTextureUrl` (it is a
full interface texture, not an icon). Note this is separate from the About text's
inline `{img:}` images, which *are* rendered (including the loading-screen banner
via the override above).

## In-game layout verification

In-game formatting keeps a 550px authored canvas with 12px body text, explicit
line breaks, unpadded side images, and stretched image dimensions (including
thin decorative dividers). Frame-wide side images sit behind the following text
so authored blank lines can place headings over banners. In-game typography is
isolated from Simple View; headings have no automatically added border.
The whole canvas displays at 125% scale where space permits, matching the
reference's 688px artwork and 15px body text. Narrower panels scale the entire
canvas down together rather than stretching the text column or reflowing it.

Run the regressions with `node --test tests/*.test.cjs`.

PNG export captures a separate snapshot, embeds available artwork, and leaves
missing images blank instead of aborting the download. Font embedding falls
back to system fonts when a remote stylesheet is unavailable. Export does not
change the live profile's layout or scroll position. Banner sections reserve
the authored image height so the next section cannot overlap the artwork.

PNG exports use a fixed 1280px composition rendered at 2x resolution, with 32px
outer margins and a consistent sidebar. View tabs, font controls, and editing
controls are removed from the snapshot. Section icons are inline SVG and do
not depend on Font Awesome embedding. The map banner, replacement Deceitful
icon, and question-mark fallback are bundled and embedded as data URLs.

Export first captures pixels from the original displayed images, then reuses a
bounded cache of embedded data. Supported WoW image CDNs load with anonymous
CORS so those pixels remain readable. A legacy wiki banner URL resolves to the
bundled game artwork if its displayed pixels are not origin-clean. Only images
without readable pixels or embedded data require a cache-preferring fetch.

The app bar contains Recent profiles, Appearance, and Import profile. After an
import, the profile header shows the character name, edit status, full-screen
preview, and an Export profile menu with PNG, Discord, and TRP3 options. The
About panel switches between Reader view and In-game style. Export menus close
with Escape and return keyboard focus to their trigger.

## Bundled artwork sources

Artwork is embedded in `assets.js`; the names below are resource keys, not
separate files. This keeps essential images independent of remote CORS and
hotlink restrictions. All World of Warcraft artwork belongs to Blizzard Entertainment.

- `textures/loadscreen-mappirate.webp`: game texture `Interface/GLUES/LOADINGSCREENS/Expansion09/Main/LoadScreen_MapPirate`, FileDataID 5580542, retrieved from `https://wago.tools/api/casc/5580542`. Converted from BLP to WebP at 1600px width.
- `icons/deceitful.jpg`: `ability_rogue_disguise`, retrieved from `https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/large/ability_rogue_disguise.jpg`. Replaces the unavailable legacy `inv_misc_mask_02` personality icon.
- `icons/questionmark.jpg`: `inv_misc_questionmark`, retrieved from `https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/large/inv_misc_questionmark.jpg`.
